## Testing Security Controls

### 1. Test Rate Limiting
```bash
# Test login rate limit (should block after 5 attempts)
for i in {1..10}; do
  curl -X POST "https://your-api/api/v1/Login/LoginWithDomain" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"test@example.com","password":"wrong"}'
done
```

### 2. Test File Upload Validation
```bash
# Test file size limit
curl -X POST "https://your-api/api/v1/Upload" \
  -F "file=@large_file.pdf"

# Test file extension validation
curl -X POST "https://your-api/api/v1/Upload" \
  -F "file=@malicious.exe"
```

### 3. Test Password Policy
```bash
# Test weak password (should fail)
curl -X POST "https://your-api/api/v1/Login/ResetPassword" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"test@example.com","password":"123456","token":"xyz"}'
```

